# Phase 7: spice-read: LTspice .tran startup and .backanno (render::read
# testbench, cards). `.tran … startup` and `uic` are read in any order
# (LTspice help, .TRAN modifiers) into the transient (`startup`): LTspice
# writes `.tran <step> <stop> [UIC] startup`, every other simulator refuses
# W0037 (no start-up ramp; ngspice's RAMPTIME is not shown to be the same
# ramp, FINDINGS-spice-read.md). `.backanno` (LTspice help: the viewer's
# port-current names, no number of the run) is left out on every target
# with the note W0036. So every LTspice deck's LTspice text changes (no
# .backanno line; .tran now an analysis, written after the raw lines), CDL
# loses the two copied lines, and a deck whose only foreign line was one of
# them is written where it was refused (W0001). Oracle: the LTspice help
# clauses (no LTspice binary); the ngspice decks written are the source's
# elements and analyses, by reading.
