# Phase 7: spice-read: Xyce .global_param, bare .ic pairs, .dc DEC/OCT/LIST,
# .step list, .tran NOOP, G/F M=, T F=/NL= (render::read testbench, sweeps,
# refused, cards, elements; lexicon/xyce.rs; spice writer's .param head).
# Xyce's .global_param is a top-level .param, which Xyce writes back as
# .global_param (Xyce 7.10 runs a constant instance temp={…} from a .param
# at the swept temperature: BUG_1203_SON/dot_step.cir), unless its value
# reads temp, vt, freq, hertz or time, itself or through another
# .global_param (Xyce runs it otherwise as a .param:
# BUG_1043_SON/RC_AC_params_analytic.cir), which stays Xyce's text. `.ic 1
# 1.0` is `.ic V(1)=1`; `.tran … NOOP` is UIC (Xyce runs both alike); a .dc
# axis by DEC/OCT or LIST (Xyce, LTspice) is Ana::DcAxes: Xyce and LTspice
# write `.dc DEC src a b n` / `src LIST v…`, HSPICE `src DEC n a b` / `src
# POI n v…`, ngspice and ESPice refuse W0038 (.dc is linear only), Spectre
# and VACASK W0015 (they have one, not written yet: FINDINGS-spice-read.md);
# `.step <name> list v…` (Xyce, LTspice) is written by both and refused
# W0016 where no .step is; `G … M=m` is the gain times m (Xyce, ngspice
# agree: -0.2 V both); `T … F=f NL=nl` is TD=nl/f (ngspice runs both
# alike). Xyce's own analyses and Y devices (.mpde .mor .pce
# .embeddedsampling, YNEURON …) refuse W0039, not W0001 (status-only here).
# Oracle: Xyce 7.10 ran each Xyce corpus deck holding one of these (noise
# list out), as given and as written for Xyce, every .prn column equal to
# 1e-6 of its scale (counts in the commit message).
