# Phase 7: spice-read: Xyce .DC LIN, R/C/L model before the value, K over
# three or more inductors, Xyce .SENS and Xyce-only cards (render::read
# sweeps, testbench, elements, refused; spice/cards.rs C/L model order;
# capability XyceSens). `.DC LIN src a b c` is the linear .dc (Xyce RG
# .DC). Xyce's `R1 a b RMOD 1k` reads as value then model when the model
# holds only TC1/TC2/TNOM and the card only TEMP/IC/M/TC1/TC2 (Xyce's
# model R/C/L multiply the value, ngspice's do not: Xyce 7.10 10 mH,
# ngspice-45 5 mH; such a card stays text); a C or L model is written
# before the value (ngspice-45: `C1 1 0 1u CM` is "unknown parameter").
# `K1 L1 L2 L3 k` (Xyce RG, LTspice help) is every pair: Xyce and LTspice
# write one card, the others one per pair (`K1`, `K1_2`, …); LTspice's
# implicit Rser=1m now skips the inductors such a K couples. Xyce .SENS
# refuses W0015 (ngspice .sens: one output, op or AC), .PREPROCESS,
# .RESULT and YPDE W0039 (status only here). Oracle: Xyce 7.10 on the
# original vs ngspice-45 on the written deck (counts in the commit).
