# Phase 7: spice-read: an LTspice .lib or .include path with blanks
# (render::read cards). LTspice has no sections (LTspice help, .LIB
# <filename>): `.lib C:\users\brian\My Documents\…\standard.dio` is one
# file, read before as file `C:\users\brian\My`, section `Documents\…`
# and written so (a wrong file on every target but LTspice). It is now a
# whole-file .lib: W0005 on the SPICE targets, W0110 on Spectre and VACASK.
# 47 lines of the sections above ("now written" for decks so read) are
# gone: those decks are refused again, as in the baseline (status only).

# Phase 7: spice-read: a given ngspice deck's `.control` `pre_osdi file`
# (render::read mod.rs) is the deck's OSDI load (ngspice manual,
# pre_osdi), dropped before with a W0025 note: ngspice writes it back,
# VACASK as `load`, ESPice, HSPICE and Xyce refuse W0004 (14 lines of the
# "inputs misread" section above now say so; status only, no diff).

# Phase 7: integrate: stream D's readings meet stream C's writers. A deck
# each branch alone left refused is written once both land: D reads the
# line it was refused for (LTspice .backanno left out W0036, Xyce
# .global_param, VACASK's benchmark ngspice decks read as ngspice), and C's
# writer spells what the other branch still refused (bsource, oct values,
# nested dc sweep, sectionless include, .print as save, option flags noted
# W0024, VACASK one-point sweep points=0). Per set: ltspice 156, xyce 36,
# vacask 8.
