# Phase 7: spectre-read-r2: VACASK sweeps over an operating point
# (render::read::named_control vacask_sweep). A control `sweep` over a
# source's `dc` (or `option="temp"`) by `step=`, `mode="lin" points=N` (N
# intervals), `mode="dec"|"oct" points=N` or `values=[…]` (VACASK docs
# cmd-sweep.md) before an `op` analysis is a `.dc` axis (Ana::Dc, or
# Ana::DcAxes for log/list, W0038 on ngspice); was only `points=N`, read as
# linear whatever its mode (a decade sweep was a wrong linear `.dc`), and
# kept as text otherwise (refused W0001). VACASK writes the sweep in its
# own spelling (analysis dc<N>); CDL no longer copies it. The VACASK
# writer's sweep of `temp` (render::named::vacask_bench sweep_line, a
# minimal arm) is `option="temp"`, was `instance="temp"` (no such
# instance: the run fails), which spice-bench's `.dc temp` decks reach too.
