# Phase 7: spice-read: Xyce's B source with POLY (render::read devices.rs
# b_poly; spice/checks.rs exempts it from W0032 like TABLE). `B … V={POLY(n)
# V(a[,b])…}` / `I={POLY(n) I(src)…}` is the E/G/F/H POLY card it spells
# (named `E` + `B…`): ngspice's B has no poly() (stream F's Y7), Xyce
# writes the POLY card back. Oracle: Xyce 7.10 B POLY vs E/F POLY, and Xyce
# vs ngspice (in the commit).
